A||||7||Alex2004||Heater suddenly isn't working!||||4||
Z||000000||Alex2004||12-30-2000||05:59 PM||||What do you think is wrong, it suddenly just stopped working, we tried to change the heater fan, and it didn't work, then we used a test light on  the plug, and it wasn't getting power, then we checked the fuse box, there was a fuse blown but it still isn't working! And we also tryed the heater/ac controls in the car and even hooked up another one to it and still, nothing happened. Does anyone know what's wrong? Thanks.<BR>Alex...<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 12-30-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||12-30-2000||07:40 PM||||Is the blower not working or doesn't it heat up?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||12-30-2000||07:58 PM||||The blower isn't working, it doesn't blow any air out. But it will heat up some if yuor going down the road.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||12-30-2000||08:04 PM||||Have you tested the fan motor itself?<BR>Just make a jumper wire and put +12 volts to it from a known good source of power.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||12-30-2000||08:15 PM||||We didn't jump the fan motor to something else, but we did use another fan motor and it didn't work. But we used a test light and it didn't come on (we also tested the test light) and we had the car running with the heater on, but still... The heater fan ever came on...so, what do you think it is? Is there a heater fan relay or something? I'll check the fuse again to see if it blew out again.<BR>Thanks<BR>Alex<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex2004||12-30-2000||08:41 PM||||well i just checked the fuse, and it was blown AGAIN! So i changed it, and it worked. I even checked it twice. I wonder how long it will last now? Hopefuly a while. But thanks for the info! <BR>Alex<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Phaeton||12-31-2000||02:41 PM||||The fan relay only works on high.  Inop heater blowing fuses is usually in the switch itself or motor drag.<BR>Poor bearings in the motor can cause too much power to be pulled when first turned on, especially when chilly.  Should be able to hear the motor complain if this is happening.  If the fan comes up to speed in a sluggish manner or any chattering or squeaking is heard then the motor is due for replacement.<P>Electical gremlins are 25 cent problems, but if everyone puts in 2 cents worth the answer will eventually be bought and owned.||||reg||12
Z||000007||Alex2004||12-31-2000||05:35 PM||||I replaced the heater fan motor with one off of the 86 GT parts car we had. It works fine now and is quiet!!! So thanks for the info!<BR>Alex...<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||10
